{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>And you shall make a plate of pure gold.</b> Such was the making of the ציץ: they would make a broad plate of gold two finger-widths wide, encircling from ear to ear, and write upon it two lines: קדש לה' — קדש below, לה' above, and the letters were raised. It was pierced at its two ends, with a thread of תכלת below it, from piercing to piercing, so that it would be tied with the thread against the back of the neck. And the Rabad, of blessed memory, explained: קדש, with its למ\"ד at the bottom, is at the end of the first line — and therefore it is called 'below,' because it is at the end. לה', which is 'above,' is at the head of the second line, and it is called 'above' because it is at the head of the reading and adjacent to it; and with this, the Name would be at the head of the line, so that it would be read in order: קדש לה'." "<b>And behold,</b> the ציץ is included among the eight priestly garments, yet it is not a garment but an ornament. And what the Sages, of blessed memory, always mention — 'eight priestly garments' — they go according to the majority, for seven of them are garments with which the High Priest clothes himself." "<b>And know</b> and understand that they correspond to the seven heavens, and at the end of the parashah of צו I shall explain this to you. And the ציץ of gold on his head is supreme above all of them, and it alludes to them all — to the quality about which it is written (Psalms 45:14): ״כל כבודה בת מלך פנימה ממשבצות זהב לבושה״ — and she is the tenth, and therefore the ציץ is of gold, and it was fitting to open it with קדש לה', as it is written: ״פתוחי חותם קדש לה'״ — and it is written: ״והיה על מצח אהרן״, and it is written: ״והיה על מצחו תמיד״. Now that you already know that the High Priest is a paradigm (דוגמא), and likewise all the garments he wears during the divine service — behold, they are a paradigm — therefore you will find that Scripture mentioned above, regarding the stones of the ephod upon his two shoulders: ״לזכרון״, and likewise regarding the חושן it mentions ״לזכרון לפני ה' תמיד״, and the word זכרון is a paradigm, for with him He mentions us, as it were. And if so, the priest during the divine service was encompassed and adorned by the twelve tribes — through the חושן in front of him and the ephod behind him — and by ע״ב bells of the fringe of his robe below, and the Shekhinah above, upon his head: the quality of judgment, in which lies mercy, watching over Israel. And this is the sense of ציץ — from the language of (Song of Songs 2:9): ״מציץ מן החרכים״, and that she receives from the supernal source — from the language of (Numbers 17:23): ״ויצץ ציץ״; it is the supernal one in fruit. And from this matter you should be roused to ask about the rest of the matters and about the order of donning the garments, for in it there is a great matter, teaching wonders, perfect in knowledge (תמים דעים) — and understand this."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:05:27.972122313Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}